{
  "where_we_lag": {
    "headline": {
      "text": "Pohjois-Savo lags the national value in crude multidisciplinary team meeting recording at 0.2% (95% CI 0.0–0.9; n=1/641) compared with 6.0% (893/14873) nationally.",
      "claim_ids": [
        "cty:mdt_recorded:Pohjois_Savon_hyvinvointialue",
        "nat:mdt_recorded"
      ]
    },
    "details": [
      {
        "text": "The 95% confidence interval for this crude multidisciplinary team share of 0.2% (95% CI 0.0–0.9; n=1/641) excludes the national 6.0% (893/14873), but HILMO codes only direct patient contacts and measures recording practice rather than care, whereas the KYS regional care chain document states KYS reviews every patient weekly.",
        "claim_ids": [
          "cty:mdt_recorded:Pohjois_Savon_hyvinvointialue",
          "nat:mdt_recorded",
          "bs:coverage:MDT",
          "q:39e6ba43a9",
          "reg:mdt_practice"
        ]
      },
      {
        "text": "Pohjois-Savo's crude curative treatment share is 24.5% (95% CI 21.3–28.0; n=157/641) compared with 27.0% (4009/14873) nationally, and because the 95% confidence interval includes the national value, this unadjusted figure is not distinguishable from the national benchmark.",
        "claim_ids": [
          "cty:curative:Pohjois_Savon_hyvinvointialue",
          "nat:curative"
        ]
      },
      {
        "text": "Across overlapping treatment categories within 12 months, Pohjois-Savo's crude life-prolonging treatment share of 38.7% (95% CI 35.0–42.5; n=248/641) and crude symptomatic treatment share of 51.2% (95% CI 47.3–55.0; n=328/641) have 95% confidence intervals that exclude the national values of 30.4% (4522/14873) and 39.5% (5871/14873).",
        "claim_ids": [
          "cty:life_prolonging:Pohjois_Savon_hyvinvointialue",
          "nat:life_prolonging",
          "cty:symptomatic:Pohjois_Savon_hyvinvointialue",
          "nat:symptomatic",
          "bs:coverage:Treatment_start"
        ]
      },
      {
        "text": "Public data do not measure county access times, while preliminary, unpublished national figures average 155 days from initial symptoms to treatment in Finland versus 107 days in Sweden and 67 days in Denmark, comprising 56 days of patient delay, 41 days in primary care, and 58 days in specialist care.",
        "claim_ids": [
          "bs:coverage:Symptoms",
          "bs:coverage:Primary_care_occupational_health",
          "bs:coverage:Referral",
          "bs:coverage:Treatment_start",
          "mot:total_fi",
          "mot:total_se",
          "mot:total_dk",
          "mot:patient",
          "mot:primary",
          "mot:specialist"
        ]
      }
    ]
  },
  "how_sure_are_we": {
    "headline": {
      "text": "Pohjois-Savo's crude 19.3% (95% CI 16.5–22.6; n=124/641) no-treatment-record share is below 27.5% (4089/14873) nationally, suggesting relatively complete treatment recording, though county shares remain unadjusted for age or stage.",
      "claim_ids": [
        "cty:no_treatment_record:Pohjois_Savon_hyvinvointialue",
        "nat:no_treatment_record",
        "bs:coverage:Diagnosis"
      ]
    },
    "details": [
      {
        "text": "The crude 19.3% (95% CI 16.5–22.6; n=124/641) share with no treatment record within 12 months mixes untreated patients and unrecorded treatment, and its 95% confidence interval excludes the national 27.5% (4089/14873).",
        "claim_ids": [
          "cty:no_treatment_record:Pohjois_Savon_hyvinvointialue",
          "nat:no_treatment_record",
          "bs:coverage:Treatment_start"
        ]
      },
      {
        "text": "Reading that crude 19.3% (95% CI 16.5–22.6; n=124/641) share as a data-quality signal is, by inference rather than direct evidence, consistent with relatively complete treatment recording, so the crude 24.5% (95% CI 21.3–28.0; n=157/641) curative share is less likely to be only a recording artefact.",
        "claim_ids": [
          "cty:no_treatment_record:Pohjois_Savon_hyvinvointialue",
          "nat:no_treatment_record",
          "cty:curative:Pohjois_Savon_hyvinvointialue",
          "nat:curative"
        ]
      },
      {
        "text": "A journal article reports HILMO diagnoses match the Cancer Registry for about 90% of most cancer types without assessing treatment recording, and county treatment shares remain unadjusted for stage or age, with Kuva 16 providing only national age-adjusted curative reference lines digitised from a figure at ±0.5 percentage points (26.7% for men, 26.9% for women).",
        "claim_ids": [
          "lit:hilmo_90",
          "bs:coverage:Diagnosis",
          "q:7885b0974f",
          "k16:curative:men:national",
          "k16:curative:women:national"
        ]
      },
      {
        "text": "Outpatient primary care visits are not included in the report's data and occupational health is not mentioned, while public data also lack symptom onset, referral dates, and treatment start dates, capturing imaging only indirectly in approximately 20% of diagnoses.",
        "claim_ids": [
          "bs:coverage:Symptoms",
          "bs:coverage:Primary_care_occupational_health",
          "q:323de0d90d",
          "bs:coverage:Imaging",
          "q:5eb155decc",
          "bs:coverage:Referral",
          "bs:coverage:First_specialist_visit",
          "bs:coverage:Treatment_start"
        ]
      }
    ]
  },
  "what_to_do_first": {
    "headline": {
      "text": "The team recommends publishing stage, drug, and multidisciplinary recording completeness, tracking THL 21/2016 access times with handover alerts, and naming a diagnostic contact alongside KYS referral rules.",
      "claim_ids": [
        "rec:1",
        "rec:2",
        "rec:3",
        "q:24169121a4",
        "q:37bb4c3b38",
        "q:950a2f797b"
      ]
    },
    "details": [
      {
        "text": "The team recommends publishing county recording completeness for stage, drug treatment, and multidisciplinary meetings: Pohjois-Savo's crude multidisciplinary share is 0.2% (95% CI 0.0–0.9; n=1/641) versus 6.0% (893/14873) nationally despite the KYS regional care chain document specifying weekly review for every patient, and the roadmap plans a national quality registry with 90% coverage including stage.",
        "claim_ids": [
          "rec:3",
          "cty:mdt_recorded:Pohjois_Savon_hyvinvointialue",
          "nat:mdt_recorded",
          "reg:mdt_practice",
          "bs:coverage:Diagnosis",
          "q:950a2f797b",
          "q:f07a34a300",
          "q:4a856bd695"
        ]
      },
      {
        "text": "The team recommends reporting access times from referral to treatment start using THL Ohjaus 21/2016 guidance definitions for 16 cancers and flagging stalled handovers, as the Health Care Act sets no maximum time for a cancer suspicion, the roadmap plans target access times in 2026–2028, and the Filha diagnostics guideline is due before 2030.",
        "claim_ids": [
          "rec:1",
          "thl:21_2016",
          "law:no_max",
          "q:def306014c",
          "q:8f358a9de6",
          "q:614febebf2"
        ]
      },
      {
        "text": "The team recommends maintaining the KYS regional care chain document's referral template and rule to refer persistent unexplained symptoms after a clear X-ray—supported by mentor insight that weak referrals receive lower urgency ratings—while naming a diagnostic-phase contact person, since reviewed regional pathway documents name none and the roadmap plans coordinator guidelines in 2026–2028 for county adoption in 2029–2031.",
        "claim_ids": [
          "rec:2",
          "reg:kys_template",
          "reg:kys_persistent",
          "reg:only_kys_xray",
          "mentor:kaisa_referral",
          "reg:named_contact",
          "q:abcbb06ae3",
          "q:050ee09ebe"
        ]
      }
    ]
  }
}
